attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 12, `tnaC` to `yidA`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 11% of calls {S1}. The model names 88 to 99.6% of them, fewest at column 1, `mnmE`, 88% {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at `yidX`**, column 13, carried by 71% {S2.c13}. Then the `dgo` genes, columns 14 to 18, [[galactonate catabolism]], carried by 89 to 93%, the stretch most in regions of plasticity, 91 to 92% {S3, S4, P, Q}. Through columns 53 to 59 a branch of 7 shell families runs in 15 to 16%, [[fructose transport and aldolases]] {S10.b53}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 94 against 86%, and hesitates less there, 0.25 against 0.64 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 52, `yicJ`, a fork column, 1.38 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in the `rfa` genes**, columns 77 to 79, [[lipopolysaccharide core]] {S10, Q}. The last column is `rfaP`, in 25% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 90% of genes**, 0.44 bits on average, perplexity 1.6 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.97 against 0.22 bits, and names fewer genes, 78% against 95% {C}.

